 and poison gas the  vehicles were plentiful with the buy and  triplane aircrafts being some of the  coolest in my experience in both  aesthetic and gameplay for those who  prefer tanks there are plenty of those  as well and light and heavy versions  in-game animations showing your  character moving around the vehicle to  swap positions kept immersion levels at  an all-time high most notably there was  the addition of cavalry units which were  honestly tanky in their own right those  horses could take several bullets if not  straight up tank shells before going  down giving you ample time to swing a  saber or shoot enemies with a long-range  rifle battlefield 1 ditched the standard  revolution introduced in battlefield 4  but added its own twist with the use of  behemoths which were a new gameplay  mechanic behemoths took on three forms  they appeared either as an armored train  dreadnought or zeppelin and were used as  a climactic form of support for the  losing side during a battle in  operations for example if a defending or  attacking team had their wave of  reinforcements wiped out a behemoth  would appear giving them a handicap for  their second wave of reinforcements  behemoths were incredibly powerful and  when destroyed particularly in the  zeppelins case took on the spectacle  that levolution used to offer in the  prior game the campaign wasn't one  cohesive story but a collection of  different accounts across different  countries and units the prologue in  particular was interesting and then as  soon as your character died you moved on  to another perspective simultaneously  putting names to the forgotten faces of  war while ironically having you  literally forget those names at the same  time as you moved between character  after character in the games you could  feel dice's symbolic nod to the  casualties of war the multiplayer maps  were awesome with plentiful locations  ranging from the western front to arabia  to the alps there were also new game  modes like war pigeons where players  would secure war pigeons and use them to  call artillery strikes operations were a  brand new mode and they were one of my  favorite battlefield modes of all time  there were super long war campaigns in  multiplayer that were similar to rush  but if the attackers captured all the  different sectors the battle would  continue onto a completely different  nearby map if you want to talk about  battlefield moments take some time to  appreciate the incredible adrenaline  rush felt when a sector was successfully  captured the transition towards the next  sector as characters in game just start  howling with planes and tanks whizzing  by on your way to the next arena but the  music swelling was nothing short of  magical just listen to this  battlefield 5 brought the fight back to  world war ii and continued the episodic  war stories instead of traditional  campaigns before we dive into some of  the other changes it is worth addressing  the elephant in the room battlefield  decided to commit to a level of realism  but got off to a shaky pr start as many  fans fixated on how unrealistic and  silly customization seemed to them while  there could be a legitimate criticism  around realism unfortunately it seems  that a subset of that group focused a  little too much on the game's inclusion  of women which seems to come from a  place of misogyny battlefield v had a  hard time shaking off this stigma and  the online internet memes and some fans  decided to boycott the game outright and  took their frustrations online the fact  remains that battlefield v although not  a smashing success wasn't nearly as  awful and horrible as many people  swearing in the comments section of the  trailer would want you to believe but  i'm also not saying that the game was  perfect the fact remains that all  battlefield games have room to improve  but i just wanted to square this away  with you guys so we can all move on  together because we have so much to be  excited about with battlefield 2042  later down the road behemoths and  levolution were gone in battlefield v  but destruction still played a heavy  role with players able to craft bunkers  and turrets with various kits to use the  maps were pretty varied with some  encouraging close quarters while other  maps represented real-life world war ii  battles such as panzerstorm a map that  had an incredible amount of tanks and  vehicles lastly there was a new battle  royale mode known as firestorm the name  represented the growing fire that took  the role of being the battle royal  mode's map boundary that progressively  began to shrink as the round continued  firestorm also featured the largest  battlefield map of all time palvoy and  the mode wasn't developed by dice  directly but by criterion games i don't  think firestorm ever took off in  popularity compared to the other modes  but i also don't know how much of that  is relative to people disliking  battlefield v as a whole for those of  you in the comments let me know if you  actually enjoyed firestorm  all right we're finally here we're  finally at the battlefield that we are  all hyped for we have plenty of really  good breakdowns on everything you need  to know about battlefield 2042 that are  super in depth but to hit the main  points battlefield 2042 brings us to a  near future setting in the game climate  change has reached its peak in  volatility and we're on route to  apocalyptic climate change now that's  all fine for the game setup but the  first thing you need to know is that  battlefield 2042 will have 128 player  servers for next-gen players which is is  just insanity to help mitigate the sheer  number of players battlefield 2042 will  have some of the biggest maps of all  time this means that conquest and flag  placements have been reworked into  clusters and sectors clusters are  specific areas of engagement designed  for players to group up and combat each  other over other flag points meanwhile  sectors are a larger group of different  clusters when all the flags are captured  then the sector in its entirety is  considered to be captured as well  specialists were introduced and are an  all-new type of fully voiced playable  soldier inspired by the traditional  battlefield classes specialists will be  equipped with individual unique traits  and a specialty with fully customizable  loadouts available there will be 10  specialists at launch with 4 planned and  upcoming seasons already revealed are  boris casper falk mckay and irish with  more details on the remaining  specialists coming later the specialties  and traits are unique and cannot be  changed for example falk is a combat  surgeon and has a trait that allows her  to revive allies to full health having  an advantage over squad revives which  take longer with not as much health  gained mckay on the other hand has a  grappling hook specialty allowing him to  quickly swing up to high ground each  squad will have four players maxed and  in conquest and breakthrough squads can  have more than one of the same  specialists 2042 will also have fully  customizable loadouts for all players  where you no longer have certain weapons  restricted based on class instead you  have access to all primary weapons  equipment such as medical crates or  anti-vehicle weapons a secondary weapon  and a throwable there's a new  tablet-based call-in system for allowing  you to call in everything from an apc to  a boston dynamics looking robodog known  as the ranger the system is based on an  allocation of team points and has a  cooldown timer there are also  environmental hazards such as emp storms  sandstorms and tornadoes all part of the  new dynamic weather system battlefield  2042 won't launch with naval warfare  according to a recent battlefield  briefing but in my mind there's room for  a potential there for dlc similar to  battlefield 4's naval strike expansion  and we already know there will be  remastered maps thanks to battlefield  portal the game will also not have an  offline mode but you can still hop in  and train with bots which are also  included in 128 player server madness  lastly battlefield 2042 has confirmed  cross-platform play being a work in  progress and that with cross-play comes  cross-progression and cross-commerce  meaning all of your purchases and  progress on one platform will carry over  on a central account allowing you to  access it all on a different platform  battlefield 2042 also introduced  battlefield portal which sounds like the  ultimate fan service and every  battlefield fans dream come true in  battlefield portal you have 6 remastered  maps across 1942 bad company 2 and  battlefield 3 making their return with a  fresh and updated visual quality the  maps allow players to fully customize a  massive list of options including  pitting armies from different eras  against one another choosing what  weapons and attachments they fight with  picking when conditions what vehicles  are available and even using a logic  editor to program modes like gun game or  protect the vip some of the modes that  players can make are really funny like  an eod bot versus tank scenario or wing  suits versus aircraft the destruction is  ramped up and is an added element to  some of the maps that might never have  had destruction on them before such as  battlefield 1942's el alamine they're  also updating maps to factor in the  larger lobbies of 2042 giving bad  company 2's valparaiso map a new low  tide area for instance to help create  more surface area for players favorite  weapons such as the tracer dart make  their return as well and with all of the  maps being developed onto the latest  edition of frostbite it is exciting to  see some of the most iconic sections of  battlefield's history fused together in  awesome combinations that exaggeration  it looks like one hell of a good time  battlefield has gone quite the distance  over the years and with all signs  pointing towards 2042 being an  action-packed hype vest i'm here for it  we've come such a long way from the  refractor engine days of battlefield  1942 and with all the lessons dice has  learned over the last two decades  hopefully battlefield 2042 will make a  significant mark in the series tell me  which battlefield game was your favorite  and why also let me know if you were a  fan of any of the smaller battlefield  games i skipped like battlefield heroes  or play for free and let me know why you  hate yourself so much if those games are  your favorite be sure to stick around  this season as we get a lot more  battlefield content coming your way  especially taking a look at the new  hazard zone it's been a blast making  these videos and it wouldn't have  happened if it wasn't for all the  excitement coming from you all in the  comments and on my twitter feed so a big  thank you i'm excited to whip up some  more videos for you guys in the future  so make sure you stick to gamespot until  next time  [Music]  you
 

